Race conditions

One challenge I faced was handling race conditions in an appointment booking application. 
For example, if two users try to book the same doctor and time slot at almost the same time, 
both requests may check the slot and see it as available, which can result in double booking.
To solve this, I don't rely only on the availability check in Node.js. I use a database transaction and 
a unique constraint on doctor, date, and time, so only one request can successfully book that slot.
If another request tries to book the same slot, the database rejects it, and I handle that error in Node.js by 
returning a 409 Conflict — slot already booked response.
This ensures that even with multiple concurrent requests, the same appointment slot cannot be booked twice.








