Garbage Collection in Node.js is the process of automatically identifying and freeing memory that is no longer being 
used by the application. Node.js uses the V8 JavaScript engine, which mainly uses a generational garbage collector. 
Short-lived objects are handled in the young generation, while long-lived objects are moved to the old generation. 
This helps prevent unnecessary memory usage, but if objects are still referenced accidentally, 
they cannot be collected and can cause memory leaks


