Zero-Downtime Deployment

I would use a rolling deployment or blue-green deployment so that the existing application continues serving traffic while 
the new version is deployed.
For example, with multiple Node.js instances behind a load balancer, I would deploy the new version to one or more instances, 
run health checks, and then gradually shift traffic to the new version.
Once the new version is stable, I would remove the old instances. If there is an issue, I can quickly route traffic 
back to the previous version.
I would also make sure database migrations are backward compatible, so old and new application versions can 
work during the deployment.


