“In payment systems, handling failures properly is very critical.

We used idempotency keys to ensure that even if a request is retried, it does not create duplicate transactions.

We also implemented retry mechanisms with exponential backoff for temporary failures.

In case of failure, we logged the error and updated the transaction status accordingly so that it can be tracked and resolved.

We also ensured that the system maintains consistency by handling partial failures properly.”

